      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q1",
      "question": "<p>A car moves in a straight line along a horizontal road with constant acceleration <span data-math=\"2\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\"></span></p><p>The car is moving with speed <span data-math=\"15\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> in the direction of the acceleration when it passes a signpost on the road.</p><p>The car is modelled as a particle.</p><p>(a) Use the model to find the speed of the car <span data-math=\"4\\,\\mathrm{s}\"></span> after passing the signpost. <strong>(2)</strong></p><p>Figure 1 below shows the horizontal forces acting on the car.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the car has mass <span data-math=\"800\\,\\mathrm{kg}\"></span></li><li>the driving force of the engine has magnitude <span data-math=\"D\"></span> newtons</li><li>the resistance to the motion of the car has magnitude <span data-math=\"400\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span></li><li>the acceleration of the car is <span data-math=\"2\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\"></span> in the direction of the driving force</li></ul><p>(b) use the model to find the value of <span data-math=\"D\"></span>. <strong>(2)</strong></p><figure><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q1-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Car of mass 800 kg; 400 N resistance to the left, driving force D N and acceleration 2 metres per second squared to the right.\" style=\"width:410px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"></figure>",
      "steps": [
        "<figure><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q1-ms-5-1.svg\" alt=\"Original Edexcel mark scheme for question 1, source page 5, section 1; working, marks and examiner guidance.\" style=\"width:700px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"></figure>",
        "<figure><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q1-ms-5-2.svg\" alt=\"Original Edexcel mark scheme for question 1, source page 5, section 2; working, marks and examiner guidance.\" style=\"width:700px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"></figure>"
      ],
      "contextHtml": "<aside class=\"exam-instructions\"><p><strong>Original paper instructions</strong></p><p>You should show sufficient working to make your methods clear. Answers without working may not gain full credit.</p><p>Unless otherwise indicated, whenever a value of <span data-math=\"g\"></span> is required, take <span data-math=\"g=9.8\\,\\mathrm{m}\\,\\mathrm{s}^{-2}\"></span> and give your answer to either 2 significant figures or 3 significant figures.</p></aside>"
