    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q2",
      "question": "<figure><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q2-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Box B of mass 2 kg on a horizontal plane, pulled by a 5 N force at angle alpha above the plane.\" style=\"width:440px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"></figure><p>A small box <span data-math=\"B\"></span> of mass <span data-math=\"2\\,\\mathrm{kg}\"></span> is dragged in a straight line, along a rough horizontal plane, at a constant speed by a force of magnitude <span data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span>.</p><p>The line of action of the force makes an angle <span data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> with the plane, where <span data-math=\"\\sin\\alpha=\\frac35\"></span>, as shown in Figure 2.</p><p>(a) Show that the magnitude of the normal reaction of the plane on the box is <span data-math=\"16.6\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span>. <strong>(3)</strong></p><p>At the instant when <span data-math=\"B\"></span> is at the point <span data-math=\"O\"></span> on the plane, the force of magnitude <span data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span> is removed.</p><p>(b) Describe the motion of the box after the force of magnitude <span data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span> is removed. <strong>(1)</strong></p><p>(c) Find the magnitude of the normal reaction of the plane on the box after the force of magnitude <span data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span> is removed. <strong>(1)</strong></p><p>Given that after the force of magnitude <span data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span> is removed</p><ul><li>the box is modelled as a particle</li><li>air resistance is modelled as being negligible</li><li>the coefficient of friction between the box and the plane is modelled as <span data-math=\"0.2\"></span></li><li>the speed of the box as it passes through <span data-math=\"O\"></span> is <span data-math=\"4\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span></li><li>the box comes to rest at the point <span data-math=\"X\"></span> on the plane</li></ul><p>(d) use the model to find the length <span data-math=\"OX\"></span>. <strong>(4)</strong></p><p>(e) State one limitation of the model, apart from ignoring air resistance, that could affect your answer to part (d). <strong>(1)</strong></p>",
