      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q5",
      "question": "<figure><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2025-june/q5-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Stone projected from O at 14 metres per second at angle theta; O is H metres vertically above N and A is 40 metres horizontally from N.\" style=\"width:470px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"></figure><p>A small stone is projected with speed <span data-math=\"14\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> from a point <span data-math=\"O\"></span> on the top of a cliff. The point <span data-math=\"O\"></span> is <span data-math=\"H\"></span> metres vertically above the point <span data-math=\"N\"></span>.</p><p>Point <span data-math=\"N\"></span> is on horizontal ground.</p><p>The stone is projected at an angle <span data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> above the horizontal, where <span data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\frac12\"></span></p><p>The stone strikes the horizontal ground at the point <span data-math=\"A\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"NA=40\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>, as shown in Figure 3.</p><p>The stone is modelled as a particle moving freely under gravity.</p><p>Using this model, find</p><p>(a) the value of <span data-math=\"H\"></span> <strong>(5)</strong></p><p>(b) the maximum height of the stone above the horizontal ground. <strong>(3)</strong></p>",
